267
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:52.000
Who is this? Oh, forget it.

268
00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:01.000
Well, it appears you have cleared
our background check,

269
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:04.000
Dr. Gru.

270
00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:08.000
Oh! And I see you have made a list

271
00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:13.000
of some of your personal achievements.

272
00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:16.000
Thank you for that.
I love reading.

273
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.000
And I see you have been given
the Medal of Honor

274
00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:29.000
and a knighthood.

275
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.000
Me, me, me. Me, me, me.

276
00:26:32.000 --> 00:26:34.000
Kevin?

277
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:37.000
You had your own cooking show

278
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:41.000
and you can hold your breath
for 30 seconds?

279
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.000
It's not that impressive.

280
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.000
Uh...

281
00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:47.000
Idiot!

282
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:52.000
Fight! Fight! Fight! Fight!

283
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:56.000
What in the name of... What?

284
00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:59.000
Well, here's the dealio.

285
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:05.000
Things have been so lonely since my wife,

286
00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:09.000
Debbie, passed on.

287
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:13.000
It's like my heart is a tooth,

288
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:18.000
and it's got a cavity that can only
be filled with children.

289
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
I'm sorry.

290
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:27.000
You are a beautiful woman.
Do you speak Spanish?

291
00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:31.000
Do I look like I speak Spanish?

292
00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:36.000
You have a face como un burro.

293
00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:39.000
Oh!

294
00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:42.000
Well, thank you!

295
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.000
Anyway, can we proceed with this adoption?

296
00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:49.000
So, so excited!

297
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:54.000
Please tell Margo, Edith and Agnes
to come to the lobby.

298
00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:58.000
I bet the mom is beautiful!

299
00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:00.000
I bet the daddy's eyes sparkle.

300
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.000
I bet their house is made of Gummi Bears.

301
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.000
I'm just saying it'd be nice.

302
00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:11.000
Aw! My caterpillar never turned
into a butterfly.

303
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.000
That's a Cheeto.

304
00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Oh!

305
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:20.000
Well, Debbie was a very lucky woman.

306
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.000
Who's Debbie?

307
00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:25.000
Your wife.

308
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:27.000
Oh! Hi, girls!

309
00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:40.000
Girls, I want you to meet Mr. Gru.

310
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:43.000
He's going to adopt you.

311
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:46.000
And he's a dentist!

312
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:50.000
Yeah!

313
00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
Um...

314
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:58.000
Hi. I'm Margo. This is Edith.

315
00:28:58.000 --> 00:28:59.000
And that's Agnes.

316
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:02.000
I got your leg, I got your leg!

317
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:05.000
Okay, that is enough, little girl.

318
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:07.000
Let go of my leg. Come on.
You can do it. Higher!

319
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:10.000
Higher! Just release your grip. Wow!

320
00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:13.000
How do you remove them?
Is there a command?

321
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:16.000
Some nonstick spray?

322
00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Crowbar?

323
00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:24.000
Okay, girls, let's go.

324
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:46.000
Ah-ha!

325
00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:49.000
Oh, yeah!

326
00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:53.000
Pretty impressive!

327
00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:56.000
What are you looking at?

328
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.000
Boo-ya!

329
00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:02.000
You got shrunk, tiny mouthwash!

330
00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:04.000
Take that!

331
00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.000
You done been shrunk!

332
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
Yello?

333
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:12.000
I got the shrink ray, all right.

334
00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:14.000
No, I'm not playing with it.

335
00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:18.000
Gru?

336
00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:20.000
Don't make me laugh! No.

337
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:23.000
P.S., he is not getting the moon,

338
00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:26.000
and P.P.S., by the time I'm done with him,

339
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:28.000
he's gonna be begging for mercy.

340
00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:32.000
Okay, bye.

341
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:38.000
Aw! Look at you, a little tiny toilet
for a little tiny baby...

342
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:41.000
Curse you, tiny toilet!

343
00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:47.000
Okay, here we are.

344
00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:49.000
Home sweet home.

345
00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:54.000
So, this is, like, your house?

346
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:56.000
Wait a sec...

347
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:59.000
You're the guy who pretended
he was a recorded message!

348
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:02.000
No, that was someone else.

349
00:31:14.000 --> 00:31:16.000
Can I hold your hand?

350
00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:18.000
Uh, no.

351
00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:30.000
When we got adopted by a bald guy,

352
00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.000
I thought this'd be more like Annie.

353
00:31:41.000 --> 00:31:44.000
No, hey!

354
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:50.000
Kyle, these are not treats.
These are guests.

355
00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:53.000
Girls, this is Kyle, my

356
00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:55.000
dog.

357
00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:59.000
Ooh! Fluffy doggy!

358
00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:04.000
What kind of dog is that?

359
00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:08.000
He is a... I don't know.

360
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:12.000
Do you really think that this is
an appropriate place for little kids?

361
00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:14.000
'Cause it's not.

362
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:17.000
No! No! Stay away from there!

363
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:19.000
It's fragile.

364
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:24.000
Well, I suppose the plan will
work with two.

365
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:28.000
Hey! It's dark in here.

366
00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:33.000
It poked a hole in my juice box.

367
00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:39.000
As you can see,

368
00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:43.000
I have provided everything
a child might need.

369
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.000
All right.

370
00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:50.000
Uh... Okay. As I was saying...
Hey!

371
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:51.000
Somebody broke that.

372
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:55.000
Okay, okay. Clearly,
we need to set some rules.

373
00:32:55.000 --> 00:32:57.000
Rule number one.

374
00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:00.000
You will not touch anything.

375
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.000
Uh-huh. What about the floor?

376
00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Yes, you may touch the floor.

377
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.000
What about the air?

378
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:08.000
Yes, you may touch the air!

379
00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:10.000
What about this?

380
00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:14.000
Where did you get that?
Found it.

381
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:18.000
Okay. Rule number two. You will not
bother me while I'm working.

382
00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:20.000
Rule number three.

383
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:25.000
You will not cry or whin or laugh or giggle

384
00:33:25.000 --> 00:33:28.000
or sneeze or burp or fart!

385
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:32.000
So, no, no, no annoying sounds.
All right?

386
00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:35.000
Does this count as annoying?

387
00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:40.000
Very!

388
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:45.000
I will see you in six hours.

389
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:51.000
Okay, don't worry.
Everything's going to be fine.

390
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:56.000
We're gonna be really happy here.
Right? Agnes?

391
00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:59.000
Mmm?

392
00:34:23.000 --> 00:34:27.000
Uh, question. What are these?

393
00:34:27.000 --> 00:34:32.000
A dozen boogie robots! Boogie!

394
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:35.000
Look at this. Watch me!

395
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:41.000
Cookie robots.
I said cookie robots.

396
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:45.000
Why are you so old?

397
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.000
Okay. I'm on it.

398
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:51.000
Hello?

399
00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:08.000
TV!

400
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.000
What is that?

401
00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Wow! Look at that!

402
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:32.000
That is cool!

403
00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:33.000
Come on!

404
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:37.000
I don't think he's a dentist.

405
00:35:50.000 --> 00:35:51.000
We've been working
on this for a while.

406
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:55.000
It's a anti-gravity serum.

407
00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.000
I meant to close that. He'll be
all right, I'm sure.

408
00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:05.000
Do the effects wear off?

409
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:07.000
Uh, so far,

410
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.000
no. No, they don't.

411
00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:14.000
And here, of course, is the new
weapon you ordered.

412
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:18.000
No, no.

413
00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:22.000
I said "dart gun," not... Okay.

414
00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:25.000
Oh, yes. 'Cause I was wondering

415
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:28.000
under what circumstances would we use this?

416
00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:29.000
But, anyway.

417
00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:34.000
What I really wanted to show you was this.

418
00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:42.000
Now those are cookie robots!

419
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:45.000
La, la, la, la I love unicorns

420
00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:49.000
What are you doing here? I told you
to stay in the kitchen!

421
00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:52.000
We got bored.
What is this place?

422
00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:54.000
Can I drink this?

423
00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:57.000
Do you want to explode?

424
00:36:58.000 --> 00:36:59.000
Gru!

425
00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:01.000
Get back in the kitchen!

426
00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:03.000
Will you play with us? No.

427
00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:06.000
Why? Because I'm busy.

428
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:07.000
Doing what?

429
00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:09.000
Um...

430
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:10.000
Okay, okay, you got me.

431
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:14.000
The dentist thing is more of a hobby.

432
00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:17.000
In real life, I am a spy.

433
00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:20.000
And it is top secret,
and you may not tell anybody,

434
00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:23.000
because if you do...
What does this do?

435
00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:28.000
Hey! Oops.

436
00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.000
My unicorn!

437
00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.000
You have to fix it.

438
00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:34.000
Fix it? Look, it has been disintegrated.

439
00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:38.000
By definition, it cannot be fixed.

440
00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:44.000
That's freaking me out.
What is she doing?

441
00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:48.000
She's gonna hold her breath
until she gets a new one.

442
00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:52.000
It is just a toy. Now stop it!

443
00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.000
Okay, okay! I'll fix it!

444
00:37:57.000 --> 00:38:00.000
Tim! Mark! Phil!

445
00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:03.000
This is very important.

446
00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:06.000
You have to get the little
girl a new unicorn toy.

447
00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:08.000
Eh?

448
00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:15.000
Hey, hey, hey! A toy!

449
00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:18.000
Go, and hurry!

450
00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:19.000
What are those?

451
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:23.000
They are my cousins.

452
00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:26.000
Jerry! Stuart!

453
00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:30.000
Watch them, and keep them
away from me, please.

454
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:49.000
Wow!

455
00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:13.000
Ooh!

456
00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:26.000
Oh!

457
00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:28.000
Hmm...

458
00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
It was your cousin's idea.

459
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:56.000
What?

460
00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:58.000
Okay, bedtime.

461
00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:00.000
Aw!

462
00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:01.000
Aw! Aw!

463
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:04.000
Not you two!

464
00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:10.000
Okey-dokey. Beddie-bye.
All tucked in. Sweet dreams.

465
00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:13.000
Just so you know,

466
00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:15.000
you're never gonna be my dad.

467
00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:18.000
Hmm. I think I can live with that.

468
00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:21.000
Are these beds made out of bombs?

469
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:26.000
Yes, but they are very old and
highly unlikely to blow up.

470
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:29.000
But try not to toss and turn.

471
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.000
Cool.

472
00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:34.000
- Will you read us a bedtime story?
- No.

473
00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:37.000
But we can't go to sleep
without a bedtime story.

474
00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:41.000
Well, then it's going to be a
long night for you, isn't it?

475
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:45.000
So, good night, sleep tight, and
don't let the bed bugs bite.

476
00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:50.000
Because there are literally
thousands of them.

477
00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:54.000
And there's
probably something in your closet.

478
00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:58.000
He's just kidding, Agnes.

479
00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:17.000
Para tu... Papoy

480
00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:22.000
It's beautiful.

481
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.000
Girls, let's go.

482
00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:55.000
Time to deliver the cookies!

483
00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:59.000
Mmm. Okay. But first,
we're going to dance class.

484
00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:02.000
Actually, we're going to have
to skip the dance class today.

485
00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:04.000
Actually, we can't

486
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:06.000
Skip the dance class today.

487
00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:08.000
We have a big recital coming up.

488
00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:10.000
We're doing an excerpt from Swan Lake.

489
00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:12.000
Yeah, Swan Lake!

490
00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.000
That's fantastic. Wonderful.

491
00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:19.000
But we're going to deliver cookies!
Come on!

492
00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:22.000
No.

493
00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:23.000
No?

494
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:26.000
We're not going to deliver
cookies until we do dance class.

495
00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:27.000
Really?

496
00:42:27.000 --> 00:42:31.000
Well, I am not driving you
to dance class.

497
00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:38.000
So if you want to go, you are
going to have to walk yourselves.

498
00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:44.000
What are you doing?

499
00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:46.000
Walking to dance class.

500
00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:48.000
Ya? Okay, fine.

501
00:42:48.000 --> 00:42:52.000
You just keep walking, because
I'm really not driving you!

502
00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:54.000
Okay.

503
00:42:55.000 --> 00:42:58.000
You're going to suffer the wrath of Gru!

504
00:42:58.000 --> 00:43:00.000
Seriously, I'm going to count to three!

505
00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.000
And you had better be in this car!

506
00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:05.000
Here we go! One! Two!

507
00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:09.000
Three, four and five.

508
00:43:09.000 --> 00:43:12.000
And lift, and stretch.

509
00:43:12.000 --> 00:43:15.000
And one, and two...

510
00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:17.000
Here you go. What is it?

511
00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:21.000
Your ticket to the dance recital.
You are coming, right?

512
00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:22.000
Of course, of course.

513
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:25.000
I have pins and needles
that I'm sitting on.

514
00:43:25.000 --> 00:43:28.000
Pinky promise?

515
00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:33.000
Oh, yes. My pinky promises.

516
00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:50.000
All right. Our first customer
is a man named Vector.

517
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:52.000
But he's a V.

518
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:54.000
You know, we're supposed
to start with the A's.

519
00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.000
Then we go to the B's.
Then we...

520
00:43:56.000 --> 00:43:58.000
Yes, yes!
I went to kindergarten.

521
00:43:58.000 --> 00:44:02.000
I know how the alphabet works!

522
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:06.000
I was just thinking

523
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:10.000
that it might be nice to
deliver Mr. Vector's first.

524
00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.000
That is all.

525
00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:18.000
Almost over. It's almost over.

526
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:25.000
Girls, welcome back to the fortress
of Vector-tude!

527
00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:28.000
Do you have my cookies for me?

528
00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:37.000
Four boxes of mini-mints,
two toffee totes,

529
00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:42.000
two caramel clumpies and
fifteen boxes of coco-nutties.

530
00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:45.000
Exactly. I'd like to see somebody
else order that many cookies.

531
00:44:45.000 --> 00:44:46.000
Not likely.

532
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:49.000
Name one person who ordered
more cookies than me.

533
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:51.000
That'll be $52.

534
00:44:51.000 --> 00:44:53.000
Right.

535
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.000
Seven, eight, nine...

536
00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:06.000
Tic Tacs! Where was I?

537
00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:09.000
Seven, eight, nine...

538
00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:11.000
Why are you wearing pajamas?

539
00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:16.000
These aren't pajamas!
This is a warm-up suit.

540
00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:35.000
What are you warming up for?
Stuff.

541
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:36.000
What sort of stuff?

542
00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.000
Super-cool stuff you wouldn't understand.

543
00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.000
Like sleeping?

544
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:44.000
They are not pajamas!

545
00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:59.000
Here you go, 52 big ones.

546
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.000
Bye!

547
00:47:11.000 --> 00:47:13.000
Come on!

548
00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:37.000
What the...

549
00:47:39.000 --> 00:47:42.000
Quiet down, fish!

550
00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:50.000
Down, boy!

551
00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:12.000
Ah-ha!

552
00:48:12.000 --> 00:48:16.000
We did it!
Come on, girls, let's go!

553
00:48:23.000 --> 00:48:26.000
But what about the other
people who ordered cookies?

554
00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:29.000
Life is full of disappointments

555
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:33.000
for some people.

556
00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:38.000
Don't do that!

557
00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:42.000
Super Silly Fun Land!
Can we go? Please?

558
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:43.000
No.

559
00:48:43.000 --> 00:48:46.000
But we've never been. And it's
the funnest place on earth!

560
00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:47.000
Don't care.

561
00:48:47.000 --> 00:48:48.000
Please? Please?

562
00:48:48.000 --> 00:48:50.000
We'll never ask for
anything else, ever again!

563
00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:53.000
Pretty please? Please?

564
00:48:59.000 --> 00:49:01.000
Come on! Come on!

565
00:49:01.000 --> 00:49:04.000
Light bulb.

566
00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:10.000
Come on!

567
00:49:10.000 --> 00:49:14.000
Goodbye, have fun.

568
00:49:17.000 --> 00:49:20.000
Sorry, dude. They can't
ride without an adult.

569
00:49:20.000 --> 00:49:23.000
What?

570
00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:20.000
Oh, my gosh!

571
00:50:20.000 --> 00:50:23.000
Look at that fluffy unicorn!

572
00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:27.000
He's so fluffy, I'm gonna die!

573
00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:29.000
You've gotta let us play for it!

574
00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:31.000
No, no, no.

575
00:50:31.000 --> 00:50:33.000
Come on!

576
00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:37.000
How much for the fluffy unicorn?

577
00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:39.000
Well, it is not for sale.

578
00:50:39.000 --> 00:50:41.000
But all you gotta do to win it

579
00:50:41.000 --> 00:50:45.000
is knock down that little spaceship there.

580
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:47.000
It's easy!

581
00:50:55.000 --> 00:50:57.000
Yay!

582
00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:10.000
Again!

583
00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:12.000
Wait! Come on. One more time!

584
00:51:12.000 --> 00:51:13.000
Just one more.

585
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:17.000
I accidentally closed my eyes.

586
00:51:31.000 --> 00:51:34.000
I hit it! I hit it!
That was cool.

587
00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:37.000
Aw!

588
00:51:38.000 --> 00:51:41.000
Whoa, whoa, whoa. What was that?

589
00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:44.000
She hit that. I saw
that with my own eyes.

590
00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:47.000
Hey, buddy, let me explain
something to you.

591
00:51:47.000 --> 00:51:50.000
You see that little tin spaceship?

592
00:51:50.000 --> 00:51:52.000
You see how it's not knocked over?

593
00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:55.000
Do you know what that means, professor?

594
00:51:55.000 --> 00:51:58.000
It means you don't get the unicorn!

595
00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:00.000
Oh! Uh-oh!

596
00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.000
Somebody's got a frowny face.

597
00:52:02.000 --> 00:52:06.000
Boo! Better luck next time!

598
00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:11.000
Okay, my turn.

599
00:52:31.000 --> 00:52:35.000
Knocked over!

600
00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:40.000
It's so fluffy!

601
00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:42.000
Yeah!

602
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:44.000
That was awesome!

603
00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:46.000
You blew up the whole thing!

604
00:52:46.000 --> 00:52:49.000
Let's go. Let's try another game!

605
00:52:55.000 --> 00:52:58.000
Gru, do you mind
if I have a quick word?

606
00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:01.000
Okay, girls, go play.

607
00:53:08.000 --> 00:53:11.000
I got the shrink ray!

608
00:53:13.000 --> 00:53:16.000
Cotton candy!

609
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:20.000
We have 12 days until the
moon is in optimum position.

610
00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:23.000
We can't afford any distractions!

611
00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:26.000
Get me Perkins.

612
00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:33.000
Ah-ha!

613
00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:35.000
Sorry to bother you,
Mr. Perkins,

614
00:53:35.000 --> 00:53:40.000
but I figured that you
would want to see this!

615
00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:42.000
What?

616
00:53:54.000 --> 00:53:55.000
Well done, Gru.

617
00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:56.000
Rather impressive.

618
00:53:56.000 --> 00:54:00.000
Now, the rest
of the plan is simple.

619
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:04.000
I fly to the moon.
I shrink the moon.

620
00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:08.000
I grab the moon.
I sit on the toilet.

621
00:54:08.000 --> 00:54:09.000
What?

622
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:12.000
Sorry. Sorry!

623
00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:15.000
Could you excuse me for just one second?

624
00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:16.000
I told you not to touch my things.

625
00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:19.000
I told you, I told you. I've
told you a thousand times.

626
00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:21.000
Hey, can we order pizza?

627
00:54:21.000 --> 00:54:23.000
Pizza? You just had lunch.

628
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:24.000
Not now, for dinner.

629
00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:26.000
Dinner?

630
00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:29.000
Just... Fine, fine, fine, whatever.
Just get back in there!

631
00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:32.000
Oh! Can we get stuffed crust?

632
00:54:32.000 --> 00:54:33.000
Stuffed crust! Stuffed crust!

633
00:54:33.000 --> 00:54:36.000
I'll stuff you all in the crust!

634
00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:38.000
You're funny!

635
00:54:38.000 --> 00:54:42.000
Just don't come out of that room again!

636
00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:44.000
All right.

637
00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:47.000
Sorry about that. Where were we?

638
00:54:47.000 --> 00:54:49.000
You were sitting on the toilet.

639
00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:53.000
No, no, no! No, I'm sorry. It
was a little attempt at humor.

640
00:54:53.000 --> 00:54:57.000
I know how much you like to laugh

641
00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:04.000
inside. Now, I was saying...

642
00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:08.000
You don't seem
terribly focused, Gru.

643
00:55:08.000 --> 00:55:11.000
Believe me,
I am completely focused.

644
00:55:11.000 --> 00:55:13.000
Hello! Whoa! What?

645
00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:14.000
That guy is huge!

646
00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:16.000
Are we on TV?
What are those? Children?

647
00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:19.000
What are you doing? I told
you to stay out of here!

648
00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:25.000
No, no, no!

649
00:55:25.000 --> 00:55:26.000
Freeze ray!

650
00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:29.000
Mr. Gru?

651
00:55:32.000 --> 00:55:35.000
Okay.

652
00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:37.000
As I was saying...

653
00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:40.000
No need to continue.
I've seen quite enough.

654
00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:42.000
But my plan...

655
00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:43.000
Is a great plan.

656
00:55:43.000 --> 00:55:47.000
I love everything about your
plan, except for one thing.

657
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:49.000
You.

658
00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:56.000
Look, Mom, I drew a picture
of me landing on the moon!

659
00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:03.000
Look, Mom, I made a prototype
of the rocket out of macaroni!

660
00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:07.000
Look, Mom, I made a real rocket

661
00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:10.000
based on the macaroni prototype!

662
00:56:21.000 --> 00:56:23.000
I don't understand.

663
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:25.000
Let's face reality, Gru.

664
00:56:25.000 --> 00:56:30.000
You've been at this for far too
long with far too little success.

665
00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:35.000
We're gonna put our faith,
our money, into a...

666
00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:37.000
Well, a younger villain.

667
00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:38.000
But I...

668
00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:41.000
It's over. Goodbye, Gru.

669
00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:06.000
Now, I know there have been
some rumors going around

670
00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:10.000
that the bank is no longer funding us.

671
00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:14.000
Well, I am here to put those
rumors to rest.

672
00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:17.000
They are true.

673
00:57:17.000 --> 00:57:19.000
Uh-oh!

674
00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:22.000
In terms of money,

675
00:57:23.000 --> 00:57:25.000
we have no money.

676
00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:28.000
So how will we get to the moon?

677
00:57:29.000 --> 00:57:30.000
The answer is clear.

678
00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:33.000
We won't.

679
00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:38.000
We are doomed.

680
00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:41.000
Now would probably be a good time

681
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:44.000
to look for other employment options.

682
00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:46.000
I know.

683
00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:53.000
I have fired up my resume as I
suggest that all of you do, as well.

684
00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:55.000
What is it?

685
00:57:56.000 --> 00:58:00.000
Can't you see that I am in
the middle of a pep talk?

686
00:58:29.000 --> 00:58:31.000
Yes!

687
00:58:31.000 --> 00:58:34.000
Yes, we will build our own rocket

688
00:58:34.000 --> 00:58:38.000
using this and whatever
else we can find!

689
00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:42.000
Grab everything! Hit the junkyards!
Take apart the cars!

690
00:58:42.000 --> 00:58:44.000
Who needs the bank?

691
00:58:44.000 --> 00:58:47.000
Let's go. Let's go!

692
00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:38.000
Mom! What are you doing here?

693
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:41.000
And here he is in the bathtub.

694
00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:44.000
Oh! Look at his little buns.

695
00:59:46.000 --> 00:59:47.000
Mom.

696
00:59:47.000 --> 00:59:50.000
Not cool.

697
00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:55.000
And here, he's all dressed
up in his Sunday best.

698
00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:57.000
He looks like a girl!

699
00:59:57.000 --> 01:00:01.000
Yes, he does. An ugly girl!

700
01:00:23.000 --> 01:00:26.000
You're funny!

701
01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:42.000
Yes! Mine's shaped like a dead guy!

702
01:00:59.000 --> 01:01:02.000
Mr. Perkins, your son is here.

703
01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:05.000
Send him in.

704
01:01:05.000 --> 01:01:08.000
Hey, Dad.

705
01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:09.000
You wanted to see me?

706
01:01:09.000 --> 01:01:11.000
Yes, I did, Victor.

707
01:01:11.000 --> 01:01:12.000
I am not Victor anymore.

708
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:16.000
Victor was my nerd name.
Now I am Vector!

709
01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:18.000
Sit down!

710
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:21.000
Do you know where the shrink ray is?

711
01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:24.000
Duh! Back at my place.

712
01:01:24.000 --> 01:01:26.000
Oh, is that right? Back at your place?
Oh, that's cool.

713
01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:32.000
I guess Gru must just have one
that looks exactly like it!

714
01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:37.000
Oh! What the...
Those girls sold me cookies!

715
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:41.000
Do you have any idea how lucrative
this moon heist could be?

716
01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:43.000
I give you the opportunity of a lifetime,

717
01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:45.000
and you just blow it!

718
01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:48.000
No, I didn't.

719
01:01:48.000 --> 01:01:49.000
Oh, really?

720
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:52.000
You just wait until Gru sees
my latest weapon.

721
01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:56.000
Squid-launcher! Oh, yeah!

722
01:01:57.000 --> 01:02:01.000
There's a squid on my face!

723
01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:03.000
Don't worry.

724
01:02:03.000 --> 01:02:07.000
The moon is as good as ours.

725
01:02:09.000 --> 01:02:11.000
Come on now, it's bedtime.

726
01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:14.000
Did you brush your teeth?
Let me smell. Let me smell.

727
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:16.000
You did not!

728
01:02:16.000 --> 01:02:20.000
Put on your PJs. Hold still.
Okay, seriously! Seriously!

729
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:23.000
This is beddie-bye time,
right now.

730
01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:25.000
I'm not kidding around.
I mean it!

731
01:02:25.000 --> 01:02:26.000
But we're not tired!

732
01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:27.000
Well, I am tired.

733
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:31.000
Will you read us a bedtime story?

734
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:35.000
No.

735
01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:36.000
Pretty please!

736
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:40.000
The physical appearance of the
"please" makes no difference.

737
01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:42.000
It is still no, so go to sleep.

738
01:02:42.000 --> 01:02:45.000
But we can't. We're all hyper!

739
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:49.000
And without a bedtime story, we'll
just keep getting up and bugging you.

740
01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:51.000
All night long.

741
01:02:52.000 --> 01:02:55.000
Fine.

742
01:02:55.000 --> 01:02:58.000
All right, all right.
Sleepy Kittens.

743
01:02:58.000 --> 01:03:00.000
Sleepy Kittens?

744
01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:02.000
- What are these?
- Puppets.

745
01:03:02.000 --> 01:03:05.000
You use them when you tell the story.

746
01:03:11.000 --> 01:03:14.000
Okay, let's get this over with.

747
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:16.000
"Three little kittens loved to play,

748
01:03:16.000 --> 01:03:19.000
"they had fun in the sun all day.

749
01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:21.000
"Then their mother came out and said,

750
01:03:21.000 --> 01:03:23.000
"'Time for kittens to go to bed."'

751
01:03:23.000 --> 01:03:27.000
Wow! This is garbage.
You actually like this?

752
01:03:27.000 --> 01:03:29.000
Keep reading!

753
01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.000
Come on! All right,
all right, all right.

754
01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:35.000
"Three little kittens started to bawl,

755
01:03:35.000 --> 01:03:37.000
"'Mommy, we're not tired at all.'

756
01:03:37.000 --> 01:03:40.000
"Their mother smiled and said with a purr,

757
01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:43.000
"'Fine, but at least you should
brush your fur."'

758
01:03:43.000 --> 01:03:47.000
Now you brush the fur.

759
01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:49.000
This is literature?

760
01:03:49.000 --> 01:03:53.000
A 2-year-old could have written this.
All right.

761
01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:56.000
"Three little kittens with fur all brushed

762
01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:59.000
"said, 'We can't sleep,
we feel too rushed! '

763
01:03:59.000 --> 01:04:03.000
"Their mother replied, with
a voice like silk,

764
01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:06.000
"'Fine, but at least
you should drink your milk."'

765
01:04:06.000 --> 01:04:09.000
Now make them drink the milk.

766
01:04:12.000 --> 01:04:16.000
I don't like this book.
This is going on forever.

767
01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:20.000
"Three little kittens,
with milk all gone,

768
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:24.000
"rubbed their eyes and started to yawn.

769
01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:32.000
"'We can't sleep, we can't even try.'

770
01:04:32.000 --> 01:04:35.000
"Then their mother sang a lullaby.

771
01:04:35.000 --> 01:04:38.000
"'Good night kittens, close your eyes.

772
01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:41.000
"Sleep in peace until you rise.

773
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:44.000
"'Though while you sleep, we are apart,

774
01:04:44.000 --> 01:04:50.000
"'your mommy loves you
with all her heart."'

775
01:04:53.000 --> 01:04:56.000
The end. Okay, good night.

776
01:04:56.000 --> 01:04:58.000
Wait!

777
01:04:58.000 --> 01:04:59.000
What?

778
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:02.000
What about good night kisses?

779
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:08.000
No, no. There will be no kissing
or hugging or kissing.

780
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:13.000
He is not gonna kiss us good night, Agnes.

781
01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:15.000
I like him. He's nice.

782
01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:17.000
But scary.

783
01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:20.000
Like Santa!

784
01:05:37.000 --> 01:05:42.000
Only 48 hours till the launch,
and all systems are go.

785
01:05:43.000 --> 01:05:46.000
Uh... About that,

786
01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:50.000
I was thinking that maybe we could
move the date of the heist.

787
01:05:50.000 --> 01:05:53.000
Please tell me this is not as a result

788
01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:56.000
of the girls' dance recital, is it?

789
01:05:56.000 --> 01:05:58.000
No, no, no!

790
01:05:58.000 --> 01:06:01.000
The recital? Don't...
That's stupid!

791
01:06:01.000 --> 01:06:06.000
I just think it's kind of
weird to do it on a Saturday.

792
01:06:06.000 --> 01:06:13.000
I was thinking, maybe a heist
is a Tuesday thing, right?

793
01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:16.000
Gru, you and I have been
working on this for years.

794
01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:18.000
It's everything we've dreamed of.

795
01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:20.000
Your chance to make history,

796
01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:24.000
become the man
who stole the moon!

797
01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:28.000
But these girls are becoming
a major distraction!

798
01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:30.000
They need to go.

799
01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:35.000
If you don't do something
about it, then I will.

800
01:06:35.000 --> 01:06:38.000
I understand.

801
01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:42.000
Good.

802
01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:46.000
Butt.

803
01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:51.000
